---
import { skillGroups } from '../data/portfolio';
---

<section id="about" class="section wrap about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">02 / About & education</p><h2 id="about-title">
        Theory meets practice.
      </h2>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="about-grid">
    <div class="about-copy">
      <p class="lead">
        I like understanding how software works beneath the surface—and using
        that understanding to build things that are useful.
      </p><p>
        I’m studying BEng Computer Science at the University of Edinburgh. My
        interests span full-stack development, machine learning, algorithms,
        computer systems, and the architecture behind databases. Financial
        technology is a particularly interesting place for me to connect
        software with analytical thinking.
      </p><p>
        Alongside my degree, I build independent projects and experiment with
        ideas beyond the syllabus. My technical work also includes C and MIPS
        assembly, stack-based parsing and syntax checking, object-oriented
        programming, and data analysis with Python and pandas.
      </p><p class="personal">
        Away from the keyboard: skiing, travelling, fitness, and cooking. I
        speak English, Spanish, and French.
      </p>
    </div><aside class="education" aria-label="Education">
      <span class="education-mark" aria-hidden="true">UoE / CS</span><p
        class="eyebrow"
      >
        Education
      </p><h3>University of Edinburgh</h3><p>BEng Computer Science</p><p
        class="muted"
      >
        2025–2029 (expected)
      </p><div class="education-grade">
        <strong>89.5<span>%</span></strong><span>First-year average</span>
      </div><p class="education-note">
        Strong academic foundations.<br />Applied through independent work.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
  <div id="skills" class="skills">
    <div class="skills-intro">
      <h3>Tools & foundations</h3><p>
        Technologies I’ve worked with across projects, experiments, and my
        degree.
      </p>
    </div><div class="skill-grid">
      {
        skillGroups.map((group) => (
          <div class="skill-group">
            <>
              <h4>{group.title}</h4>
              <ul>
                {group.items.map((item) => (
                  <li>{item}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
